Approach (Kadane’s Algorithm)
We traverse the array and keep a running sum currSum.
At each index, we add the current element to currSum.
If currSum becomes negative, we reset it to 0 (because a negative sum will reduce future subarray sums).
We maintain another variable maxSum to store the maximum subarray sum found so far.
At every step, update maxSum = max(maxSum, currSum).
Initialize maxSum with the first element to handle cases where all elements are negative.

Complexity
Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)
